    <!-- The last line of both cards on Home, whenever bedtime is not actually
         running. Every switch above them is a PLAN - written to prefs on the
         tap and applied when the window opens - and with bedtime off, turning
         Do Not Disturb "on" silences nothing tonight while looking exactly like
         a switch that would. No budget: these wrap inside a full-width card.

         Positively framed - they say when the settings WILL work rather than
         that they do not. "None of this is in effect until X" is a double
         negative a reader has to unpick, and it was reported as such. They also
         say "these settings" rather than "this" or "none of this": the strip
         sits ABOVE the rows it qualifies now, so any wording that points
         backwards would be false. See the note about text that points at its
         neighbours travelling badly. -->
    <string name="note_off">Bedtime is off. These settings take effect once you turn it on.</string>
    <string name="note_until">These settings take effect at %1$s %2$s.</string>
    <string name="note_unscheduled">No nights are scheduled, so these settings never run.</string>

