    <!-- The one readout in the app that is not the app's own belief: it reports
         what getCurrentInterruptionFilter ANSWERED, which is the whole premise
         here - a vendor can accept a request and quietly ignore it.

         It is a status PILL plus a sentence now: the pill is the verdict at a
         glance, the sentence is what that means. Before this the pill did not
         exist and the FAILURE case was signalled by colour alone - and worse,
         by the wrong words. Do Not Disturb asked for and the phone reporting
         everything getting through printed "Do Not Disturb is off. Everything
         is allowed.", which is the opposite of what happened: it was not off,
         it was ignored. filter_ignored exists for exactly that case.

         BUDGET-EACH 18 filter_pill_on filter_pill_off filter_pill_ignored
         filter_pill_alarms filter_pill_none filter_pill_unknown -->
    <string name="filter_pill_on">In effect</string>
    <string name="filter_pill_off">Off</string>
    <string name="filter_pill_ignored">Not in effect</string>
    <string name="filter_pill_alarms">Alarms only</string>
    <string name="filter_pill_none">Total silence</string>
    <string name="filter_pill_unknown">Unknown</string>
